# Undeclared-import gate allowlist (scripts/check_undeclared_imports.py).
# See docs/evidence/2026-07-27-undeclared-import-gate.md.
#
# Format: <module_name>::<repo-relative file glob>  # justification
# (required -- unjustified entries, or entries with no file-glob scope,
# are a hard error; see load_allowlist() in the gate script). The file
# glob is required so an entry can only exempt the specific file(s) it
# names, never every future use of that module anywhere in the scanned
# trees.
#
# Entries here are known, real, pre-existing gaps pending an owner
# decision -- not permission to keep importing an undeclared module
# forever. Remove an entry once its module is properly declared (or the
# importing code is fixed/retired).

# The `jax` entries are gone and this file now has no entries at all. That is
# a real state, not an oversight: both files this gate ever exempted have been
# deleted, so nothing is exempt.
#
# 2026-07-27: the check_perf_regression.py entry was REMOVED rather than kept
# -- that script was deleted by the JAX/benders_loop retirement, so its
# exemption had become vacuous (an allowlist entry scoped to a file that no
# longer exists exempts nothing, and reads as a live gap that is already
# closed).
#
# 2026-08-04: the internal_route.py entry was REMOVED for the same reason, on
# the same precedent. It had been kept on the argument that the breakage was
# LIVE -- `make route` still invoked the script, so the documented routing
# entry point exited on ModuleNotFoundError before doing any work -- and that
# the fix was likely a one-line numpy swap (all 7 `jnp.` uses were plain array
# ops, no jit/grad/vmap). Neither premise survived: #680 re-pointed `make
# route` at scripts/route_board.py, orphaning the script from the build, and
# the undeclared `jax` import was never the only defect -- the script also
# imported a `temper_placer.routing` package that no longer exists, so no
# import swap could have revived it. It was RETIREd as import-dead in
# docs/wave4-verdicts.yaml and deleted on 2026-08-04. See
# docs/evidence/2026-08-04-wave4-residual-verdicts.md.
